Z||000000||Alex4mula||04-06-2000||08:55 AM||||Hey fellows;<BR>As far as I know four companies offer V6 headers. These are:<BR>- FOCCOA, CA USA<BR>- Fiero Shop, Ontario Canada<BR>- Fiero Conversions, Ontario Canada<BR>- Chris West ??, ?? USA<P>Which you suggest is the best most reliable to buy from? Do any of these may have them in stock? I don't want to throw $600 to anyone out there. Just ordered my 3.4. Need those soon. Your suggestions will be appreciated. Thanks.||||reg||5
Z||000001||1FST2M6||04-06-2000||11:25 AM||||Chris Wests' units are better than the sprint units just by thier numbers.. larger piping. I'll be posting dyno numbers of mine when I get back from vacation. (around the 14th) I ordered them from Chris he made them the following day and had them shipped out within 3 days... have problems with UPS but thats not his fault... (my headders dissappeared from their sights for 3 days... not on their tracking sites.. no customer relations ideas... then POOF delivered...) I took them to Engineered to have them Jet-Hot coated to give them a longer life. I'll be sure to post a pic of that too... I'd say Chris West... cause there in stock he's quick and seems to be a great guy to talk to. ||||reg||1
Z||000002||Alex4mula||04-06-2000||11:36 AM||||Do you have a phone # or something to contact him? $$Price? Thanks.||||reg||1
Z||000003||1FST2M6||04-06-2000||01:01 PM||||they were $522 shipped 3 day select. his phone # 310-305-4111  make sure you tell him how you got in touch with him... (Travis from Engineered Performance in atlanta, or From Pennocks Fiero forum) He kinda laughed when I told him about the forum but once he realizes how much throw this little group of carnuts really has he might change his tune. I'm VERY optimistic and am positive Chris' headers will be worth more than his asking price at the track, on the dyno and at the next stop light...  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">  give him a shout...  he has Stainless headers in stock too! ||||reg||1
Z||000004||1FST2M6||04-06-2000||01:03 PM||||oh yeah he's in Marina Del Rey, California||||reg||1
Z||000005||Gokart||04-07-2000||04:47 AM||||Hope you got your money for shipping back 1FST2M6. I just had to demand mine back this week cause the same "ozone" problem happened to me when I sent a 3day select to Tom to get my exhaust manifolds ported. You wouldn't believe the shipping/receiving problems I've had over the years with UPS and I'm been driving for them 10 years now! <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/redface.gif">||||reg||8
